  "raw": {
    "https://jobs.anu.edu.au/jobs/anu-talent-register-canberra-act-act-australia": {
      "title": "ANU Talent Register",
      "description": "ANU Talent Register - Canberra / ACT, ACT, Australia Privacy Statement People & Culture Information for applicants Salaries & benefits Respect and Inclusion Aboriginal & Torres Strait Islander employment Applicant Login Kiosk mode ANU Talent Register 508394 Canberra / ACT, ACT, Australia, 2601 Casual Fixed Term Add to favourites View favourites Position Description Register your interest with The Australian National University today! Classifications: Various Terms: Temporary and Fixed Term Unique temporary and fixed term job opportunities available Flexible working arrangements Experience a University setting like no other Overview The ANU Talent Register represents an exciting opportunity to build your professional skills and gain a variety of employment experiences in a diverse and complex working environment. We are seeking applicants with diverse skills and experience in Administration, Executive Support, Research and Laboratory Assistance, Finance, Information Technology, Hospitality and Customer Service based roles. Ideally, applicants should have experience with the Microsoft Office suite, possess excellent communication skills and demonstrate flexibility in their approach to working with highly collaborative and collegial teams. Applications will be matched with qualifications, skills and capabilities for upcoming temporary and fixed term vacancies across the University. If your skills and experience are matched to a vacancy, you may be invited to participate in an assessment process including attending a face to face interview and/or reference checks. Applications to the ANU Talent Register do not guarantee you an offer of employment. Your application will remain active for 6 months, at which point you will need to reapply. ANU values diversity and inclusion and is committed to providing equal employment opportunities to those of all backgrounds and identities. For more information about staff equity at ANU, visit https://services.anu.edu.au/human-resources/respect-inclusion Application Information APPLY NOW to the ANU Talent Register and join our talent community. Please ensure you upload the following documents: A current curriculum vitae (CV) including the names and contact details of at least three referees (preferably including a current or previous supervisor); A cover letter addressing your interest and suitability. For specific enquiries relating to the ANU Talent Community, please email: Casual.Register@anu.edu.au Applications will not be accepted via the above email address and should be submitted online. Please note: The successful candidate must have rights to live and work in this country and will be required to undergo a background check during the recruitment process.  An offer of employment is conditional on satisfactory results. Apply Now First Name (required) 763769b3 Last Name (required) 43688cff Email (required) 586a262a Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Job referral Know someone great for this role! Job referral Know someone great for this role! Recommended Jobs Lead Optical Specialist Canberra / ACT, ACT, 2601 Ideal for an experienced optical engineer, this position provides the chance to shape cutting-edge scientific and space technologies while supporting world-leading research and innovation. Mechanical Engineering Specialist Canberra / ACT, ACT, 2601 Join the Advanced Instrumentation and Technology Centre (AITC) to provide specialist mechanical engineering expertise supporting the design, development, validation and maintenance of advanced astronomical instrumentation for world-leading research. Senior Consultant HR Systems Operations Canberra / ACT, ACT, 2601 Oversee operational support for key HR systems, ensuring high-quality service delivery to HR and Payroll stakeholders Associate Professor/ Professor of Music Canberra / ACT, ACT, 2601 An opportunity is available for an outstanding scholar to take up a leadership position at the ANU School of Music working within a collaborative team with world-class researchers and educators. Research Assistant / Research Engineer Canberra / ACT, ACT, 2601 Work with state-of-the-art techniques on AI and Robotics, in collaboration with researchers and practitioners from universities and industry. Research Officer (Peakall) Canberra / ACT, ACT, 2601 Research Officer to perform high quality plant DNA/RNA extraction, library preparation for sequencing and molecular laboratory research support. Back to top Acknowledgement of Country The Australian National University acknowledges, celebrates and pays our respects to the Ngunnawal and Ngambri people of the Canberra region and to all First Nations Australians on whose traditional lands we meet and work, and whose cultures are among the oldest continuing cultures in human history. Contact ANU Copyright Disclaimer Privacy Freedom of Information Accessibility TEQSA Provider ID: PRV12002 (Australian University) CRICOS Provider Code: 00120C ABN: 52 234 063 906 MEMBER OF Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalise content such as job recommendations, and to analyse our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device I do not accept I accept"
    },
    "https://jobs.anu.edu.au/jobs/casual-sessional-academic-course-coordinators-school-of-culture-history-and-languages-canberra-act-act-australia-b540d81c-fa65-47ab-a869-3a4b70b101d0": {
      "title": "Casual Sessional Academic- Course Coordinators - School of Culture, History and Languages - Canberra / ACT, ACT, Australia",
      "description": "Casual Sessional Academic- Course Coordinators - School of Culture, History and Languages - Canberra / ACT, ACT, Australia Privacy Statement People & Culture Information for applicants Salaries & benefits Respect and Inclusion Aboriginal & Torres Strait Islander employment Applicant Login Kiosk mode Casual Sessional Academic- Course Coordinators - School of Culture, History and Languages Casual Sessional Academic- Course Coordinators - School of Culture, History and Languages 564047 Canberra / ACT, ACT, Australia, 2601 Casual Closing at: Nov 9 2026 - 23:55 AEDT Position Description Classification: Casual Sessional Academic Salary package: As per Casual Sessional Academic salary rates Term: Casual, commencing early-2027 In 1946, ANU was founded to help rebuild a changing world. We’re still at it, 80 years later. For generations, our people have turned curiosity into ideas that have shaped Australia and our region. Learn more about ANU, our history and the community that has shaped us: ANU at 80 . College Overview The ANU College of Asia and the Pacific (CAP) is a leading center for teaching and research on Asia and the Pacific region.  The School of Culture, History & Language (CHL) offers programs in Asian and Pacific languages, cultures, histories and societies, supporting students to develop advanced language skills and intercultural understanding. Semester 1, 2027 Opportunities The School anticipates the need for one or more Casual Sessional Academics (CSAs) to undertake course coordination, teaching and/or marking duties for the courses listed below. Course Coordination Responsibilities Successful applicants may be engaged to perform course coordination duties in accordance with the ANU Enterprise Agreement and the Higher Education Standards Framework (HESF).  Depending on the course, duties may include some or all of the following activities: course and assessment development under the supervision of the Academic Course Convenor; delivery of principal or autonomous teaching content (e.g. lectures); supplementary teaching content (e.g. tutorials), marking; participation in meetings with staff or students; and completion of mandatory training modules. Courses Position overview As a Casual Sessional Academic (CSA) you will contribute to the delivery of high-quality teaching and learning within the School.  You will work with the Academic Course Convenor and other ANU staff to students to achieve the stated learning outcomes. Applicants are required to hold qualifications and/or professional experience that are relevant to the language or discipline.  Relevant experience may include university-level teaching experience, strong academic achievement in the relevant discipline; professional experience relevant to the subject area; and language teaching proficiency appropriate to the course. ANU is committed to building a diverse and inclusive community and encourages applications from women, Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, and people from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds. For more information about inclusions and equity at ANU, please visit: https://services.anu.edu.au/human-resources/respect-inclusion Enquiries CHL Administration Team: admin.chl@anu.edu.au How to apply To be considered for this opportunity, you must complete both step 1 and step 2. Step 1 Complete the online application form . Step 2 Submit your application through the ANU recruitment portal and upload the following documents: Academic qualifications: provide copies of relevant qualifications, such as: doctoral degree, master Degree, graduate diploma, or bachelor degree Evidence of teaching experience (if applicable).  Examples may include teaching evaluations, teaching awards, or a summary of previous teaching roles. Cover letter (maximum 1 page). Please include: the preferred course(s) for which you wish to be considered; a brief summary of your teaching experience and any relevant professional experience; any previous teaching or tutoring experience at ANU (including course codes and titles) Curriculum Vitae (CV) or Resume (maximum 2 pages) Two referee reports. Referee reports should be dated within the last 12 months; and preferably include a current or former supervisor. Step 3 (only relevant for shortlisted candidates who don't have postgraduate qualifications) Applicants shortlisted for a course coordination role who do not hold an Australian Qualifications Framework (AQF)+1 qualification may be asked to complete a Professional Experience Equivalency (PEE) form. The form will be used to assess whether your qualifications and professional experience meet the requirements of the Australian Qualifications Framework (AQF) and ANU policies for teaching in higher education. Important information Applications that do not follow the instructions above, or do not include the required documents, may not be considered. Course offerings and staffing requirements may change based on student enrolments and operational needs. Applicants must have the right to live and work in Australia. Casual appointments and teaching schedule depend on enrolment numbers and operational requirements. An offer of casual employment does not guarantee a minimum number of hours. Please note: The preferred candidate will be required to complete mandatory pre-employment declarations and background checks relevant to the role they have applied for, in accordance with the Background Checking Procedure and the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-Based Violence . Recommended Jobs Senior Impact and Communications Officer (Indigenous Identified) Canberra / ACT, ACT, 2601 The Senior Impact and Communications Officer coordinates communications and impact reporting that make the Centre's research, policy and project outcomes clear and accessible, supporting the Partnerships Manager to implement the communications and media strategy, strengthen partner engagement, deliver events and demonstrate impact through accurate evidence and culturally grounded storytelling. Senior Education Advisor (Indigenous Identified) Canberra / ACT, ACT, 2601 The Senior Education Advisor supports the development and delivery of the Centre's executive education, professional development and capability-building programs, translating First Nations knowledges, research, policy and practitioner expertise into accessible, culturally grounded learning for First Nations rights holders and organisations, government, industry and other partners. Partnerships Manager (Indigenous Identified) Canberra / ACT, ACT, 2601 The Partnerships Manager develops and manages the relationships, services and engagement activities that connect First Nations communities and organisations, governments and the private sector with the Centre's research, policy and institutional capabilities, and builds the partnerships and income that support the Centre's long-term sustainability. Associate Director, Education and Professional Development (Indigenous Identified) Canberra / ACT, ACT, 2601 Working closely with the Centre Director, the Associate Director will lead the design, piloting and delivery of executive education, professional development and other capability-building initiatives. Team Lead, Data Management Canberra / ACT, ACT, 2601 Lead the Data Team at Australia’s climate simulator, ACCESS-NRI. Work at the intersection of Earth system models, climate change, high-performance computing and data. Admissions Officer Canberra / ACT, ACT, 2601 Deliver accurate admissions and student compliance support, maintaining consistent processes, communication and standards."
    },
    "https://jobs.anu.edu.au/jobs/research-fellow-or-fellow-canberra-act-act-australia-834b81da-43da-48a9-813b-ddd191cac889": {
      "title": "Research Fellow or Fellow",
      "description": "Research Fellow or Fellow - Canberra / ACT, ACT, Australia Privacy Statement People & Culture Information for applicants Salaries & benefits Respect and Inclusion Aboriginal & Torres Strait Islander employment Applicant Login Kiosk mode Research Fellow or Fellow Research Fellow or Fellow 563849 Canberra / ACT, ACT, Australia, 2601 Continuing (Contingent Funded) Closing at: Nov 25 2026 - 23:55 AEDT Position Description Classification: Academic Level B or C Salary package: $124,638 - $166,338 per annum plus 17% superannuation Term: Full-time (part-time, job share or a gradual increase in hours will be considered), Continuing (contingent funded). This position is continuing (contingent funded) . The funding that supports this project has an expected end date of 31 December 2029. In 1946, ANU was founded to help rebuild a changing world. We’re still at it, 80 years later. For generations, our people have turned curiosity into ideas that have shaped Australia and our region. Learn more about ANU, our history and the community that has shaped us: ANU at 80 The Position This role is integral to the delivery and support of the ARC Industrial Transformation Training Centre for Radiation Innovation (RadInnovate). RadInnovate aims to build new capabilities for nuclear science and radiation by training the next generation of transdisciplinary leaders through the integration of core science, technology, regulation, governance and societal values. RadInnovate is led by ANU in partnership with the University of South Australia and the University of Adelaide, and with 15 industry and government partners on co-designed research projects in the areas underpinning nuclear science, technological innovation, and regulatory and social responsiveness, to equip Australian industries with a future-ready workforce. This position will be based in the ANU School of Regulation and Global Governance (RegNet) and will undertake independent research on RadInnovate’s codesigned industry projects, predominantly in the areas of regulation and social licence, and publishing original and innovative results in top-tier refereed journals. The position will co-supervise RadInnovate Higher Degree Research (HDR) students, teach into postgraduate programs in regulation and governance, and act as an interface between the HDR students and ITTC University and industry partners. The position will spend some time in industry as part of the students’ industry placements and will be involved in all-of-centre activities and in the life of the project. The Person We are looking for a strong team player with excellent interpersonal skills and the ability to work independently on high-quality research in collaboration with RadInnovate Chief Investigators. They will have a demonstrated ability as a teacher and a willingness to grow their skills to provided world-class co-supervision of HDR students. Highly developed organisational skills and effective self-management are key. We are looking for someone with a PhD in a law, regulation or a related field with a focus on regulating nuclear materials and technologies or regulating emerging technologies. Learn more about the ground-breaking research and work class facilities of the School of Regulation and Global Governance (RegNet) here . For more information about the position please contact Professor Veronica Taylor, Centre Chief Investigator on T: 0431 665 374, E: veronica.taylor@anu.edu.au Working at ANU This is an opportunity to work with a world class University that undertakes cutting edge research and has a strong tradition in research-led teaching excellence. Flexible working arrangements including hybrid arrangements working both on our beautiful, green campus and working remotely; Generous paid parental leave entitlements of up to 32 weeks. We are one of the leading employers in Australia for parental leave entitlements; Career support, training, mentoring & upskilling opportunities . For more information on a range of lifestyle, financial and non-financial rewards and programs, please click here . A Diverse and Inclusive Team ANU is introducing measures to support the recruitment, inclusion and retention of employees with disability. To find out more, please click here . ANU is a large, diverse employer with staff working across numerous professions (see the full list of available roles here . We are a recipient of the bronze award through the Science in Australia Gender Equity (SAGE) program and a platinum member of the Australian Network on Disability. We welcome applications from people of all backgrounds and identities and from individuals who may have had a non-linear career path, career gaps or career breaks. To Apply To be considered for this position, please upload the following documents: A current curriculum vitae (CV), and No more than a two-page summary addressing your suitability against the selection criteria. If shortlisted, candidates will be asked to complete a: up to 45-minute interview using technical and behavioural interview questions If you require adjustments to participate in any of the above assessments, please contact our HR team at E: recruitment@anu.edu.au . Any adjustment request or the disclosure of disability will not be communicated to the selection committee without the candidate’s consent and it will not have any bearing on hiring decisions. For examples of common reasonable adjustments please click here . Please note: The preferred candidate will be required to complete mandatory pre-employment declarations and background checks relevant to the role they have applied for, in accordance with the Background Checking Procedure and the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-Based Violence . Recommended Jobs Digital Workspace Developer Canberra / ACT, ACT, 2601 Lead secure M365 and Power Platform management and digital workspace innovation across the Australian National University. Senior Digital Workspace Developer Canberra / ACT, ACT, 2601 Lead secure M365 and Power Platform management and digital workspace innovation across the Australian National University. International Stakeholder Coordinator Canberra / ACT, ACT, 2601 Apply your reporting systems knowledge to support international student recruitment through agent contract management, compliance and performance reporting. Sponsored Students Officer Canberra / ACT, ACT, 2601 Be part of a dedicated sponsored student-facing team. Manager, Curriculum Architecture Canberra / ACT, ACT, 2601 Lead curriculum governance and quality improvement, provide expert academic policy advice, and enhance teaching and student experience. Recruitment Officer Canberra / ACT, ACT, 2601 Support recruitment across the University, partner with stakeholders, and deliver smooth, compliant hiring outcomes in a collaborative, people-focused environment. Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalise content such as job recommendations, and to analyse our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device I do not accept I accept"
    },
