    "https://jobs.anu.edu.au/jobs/postdoctoral-fellow-canberra-act-act-australia-66b61451-369b-4c02-a512-6b34c32dff95": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Fellow",
      "description": "Postdoctoral Fellow  - Canberra / ACT, ACT, Australia Privacy Statement People & Culture Information for applicants Salaries & benefits Respect and Inclusion Aboriginal & Torres Strait Islander employment Applicant Login Kiosk mode Postdoctoral Fellow Postdoctoral Fellow 563974 Canberra / ACT, ACT, Australia, 2601 Fixed Term Closing at: Nov 8 2026 - 23:55 AEDT Position Description Classification: Academic Level A Salary package: $91,546 - $114,906 per annum plus 17 % superannuation Term: Full-time, Fixed Term (up to 3 years) In 1946, ANU was founded to help rebuild a changing world. We’re still at it, 80 years later. For generations, our people have turned curiosity into ideas that have shaped Australia and our region. Learn more about ANU, our history and the community that has shaped us: ANU at 80 The Position This is a three-year, research-intensive Postdoctoral Fellow appointment supported by an ANU–BHP collaborative project. The appointee will conduct experimental and analytical research on salt melts in iron oxide copper-gold systems. The appointee will contribute primarily to research, with minor service, laboratory and project responsibilities, and may assist with research student supervision where relevant. The appointment is expected to commence in 2027, subject to the final employment arrangements. The Person The Postdoctoral Fellow will be a member of the Research School of Earth Sciences and will work under the supervision of the project lead, Dr Michael Anenburg. The Postdoctoral Fellow will contribute cooperatively to the intellectual and laboratory life of the School and will work closely with ANU researchers, technical staff and BHP collaborators. A successful candidate will have extensive knowledge in experimental petrology methods including 1-atm gas mixing furnaces, piston cylinder apparatuses, and other similar techniques. Demonstrated experience in mineralogical microanalytical techniques (e.g., SEM-EDS, EPMA-WDS, LA-ICP-MS, FTIR) is required. The School The Research School of Earth Sciences is a leading centre of Earth sciences research in Australia. Its researchers combine experimental, analytical and field-based approaches to understand Earth processes and address challenges in mineral resources and sustainable resource development. The College The ANU College of Science and Medicine encompasses the following disciplines: Astronomy and Astrophysics, Biology, Chemistry, Earth Sciences, Physics, Medicine and Psychology, and Medical Research. It is also home to various cross-disciplinary and specialist institutes and centres. Staff and students within the ANU College of Science and Medicine conduct research and deliver research-led education programs spanning the entire breadth of the sciences, supported by extensive international networks and world-class facilities. For further information please contact, Michael Anenburg, E: michael.anenburg@anu.edu.au . ANU values diversity and inclusion and is committed to providing equal employment opportunities to people of all backgrounds and identities. For more information about staff equity at ANU, click here . For enquiries about the application process, or if you require reasonable adjustment to apply for this role, please contact the hiring manager on the above listed details. Application information In order to apply for this role please make sure that you upload the following documents: A statement addressing the selection criteria (up to 2 pages). A current curriculum vitae (CV) which includes the names and contact details of at least three referees (preferably including a current or previous supervisor). If your CV does not include referees you can complete these online when prompted in the application form. Optional cover letter (up to 1 page). Applications which do not address the selection criteria may not be considered for the position. Please note: The preferred candidate must have rights to live and work in Australia and will be required to complete mandatory pre-employment declarations and background checks relevant to the role they have applied for, in accordance with the Background Checking Procedure and the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-Based Violence . Recommended Jobs Casual Course Coordinator - Coral Bell School of Asia and the Pacific Canberra / ACT, ACT, 2601 Join ANU's Coral Bell School as a Casual Course Coordinator in Semester 1, 2027, supporting teaching, assessment and student learning. Senior Research Officer Canberra / ACT, ACT, 2601 This position provides high-level digital archive curation and historical research support for a major consultancy with the Eastern Maar Aboriginal Corporation. Fellow Canberra / ACT, ACT, 2601 The School of Regulation and Global Governance is looking for an outstanding early career scholar to join us to delivery and support of the ARC Industrial Transformation Training Centre for Radiation Innovation (RadInnovate). Research Assistant Canberra / ACT, ACT, 2601 Contribute to an innovative NHMRC funded psychology project on social identity, connection, and loneliness. Manager, Compliance Canberra / ACT, ACT, 2601 Lead compliance, regulatory risk management and assurance for ANU One, ensuring pathway programmes meet legislative and regulatory standards. Deputy Manager, Outreach and Communications Canberra / ACT, ACT, 2601 Coral Bell School of Asia Pacific Affairs is looking for an experienced communications professional to lead communications, outreach and engagement."
    },
    "https://jobs.anu.edu.au/jobs/postdoctoral-research-fellow-canberra-act-act-australia-db5f1e24-2a91-430f-ace5-6d82cc90e000": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral / Research Fellow",
      "description": "Postdoctoral / Research Fellow - Canberra / ACT, ACT, Australia Privacy Statement People & Culture Information for applicants Salaries & benefits Respect and Inclusion Aboriginal & Torres Strait Islander employment Applicant Login Kiosk mode Postdoctoral / Research Fellow Postdoctoral / Research Fellow 563930 Canberra / ACT, ACT, Australia, 2601 Continuing (Contingent Funded) Closing at: Nov 15 2026 - 23:55 AEDT Position Description Classification: Academic Level A/B Salary package: $91,546 - $141,317 per annum plus 17% superannuation Term: Full-time, Continuing (Contingent Funded). This position is continuing (contingent funded) . The funding that supports this project has an expected end date of 30 June 2030. In 1946, ANU was founded to help rebuild a changing world. We’re still at it, 80 years later. For generations, our people have turned curiosity into ideas that have shaped Australia and our region. Learn more about ANU, our history and the community that has shaped us: ANU at 80 The Position Applications are sought for a Postdoctoral/Research Fellow in observational seismology. The successful applicant will join a vibrant and collaborative environment in Solid Earth Geophysics with world-class expertise in seismology, geodynamics, mathematical geophysics, and rock/mineral physics. The role will focus on passive-seismic imaging of upper mantle structure beneath the WA-Array, a continental scale array that aims cover the entirety of Western Australia at 40km station spacing over the coming decade. The goals of the project are to apply (i) anisotropic receiver functions, and (ii) S-wave Receiver Functions to study upper mantle discontinuities such as the Lithosphere-Asthenosphere Boundary. Candidates with relevant experience in observational seismology are encouraged to apply. The Person We are looking for an early career researcher with a PhD (or awarding of a PhD within six months of appointment) in the field of observational seismology (or a related area), and that has the ability to articulate and prosecute innovate research. Evidence of experience that is relevant to some or all of the following areas would be advantageous: Requesting, processing, and analysing passive-seismic data Programming skills (such as with Python or MATLAB) for data computation and visualisation Methods for imaging or probing the Earth’s upper mantle, in particular using receiver functions Prior experience of working with large datasets (e.g. from continental-scale arrays) The School The Postdoctoral/Research Fellow will be based at the Research School of Earth Sciences (RSES). RSES is Australia’s leading academic research institution for Earth and Marine Sciences, and ranked 20th in the world for Geophysics, as well as Earth and Marine Sciences ( QS World University Rankings by Subject 2026 ). To find out more about the RSES community, check out our Instagram . We have a reputation for international leadership and innovation, focused on developing new methods, whether experimental, analytical or computational. Our research spans the range from solid earth evolution to climate processes, and from 21st century resources to climate change impact. We operate iconic and state-of-the art instrumentation supported by highly trained professional staff, offering an unrivalled world-class research environment. Our cutting-edge research provides an unparalleled environment for high-quality research training of our graduate students. Our people and facilities are also the foundation for our vision to deliver world-class research-led undergraduate teaching in the Earth Sciences. We are committed to offering a nurturing environment for the School’s early career researchers. Our culture is one of inclusivity and respect and we encourage everyone to embrace these values as expressed in our culture statement . The College The ANU College of Science and Medicine encompasses the disciplines of: Astronomy, Biology, Chemistry, Earth Sciences, Environment and Society, Mathematics, Physics, and Science Communication and is also home to a number of cross-disciplinary and specialist Institutes and Centres.  Staff and students within the ANU College of Science and Medicine conduct research and deliver a research-led education program that encompasses the breadth of the sciences, supported by extensive international networks and by world-class facilities. To find out more about the Science at ANU community, follow us on social media at Instagram and Facebook For further information please contact, Dr Caroline Eakin, E: caroline.eakin@anu.edu.au. ANU values diversity and inclusion and is committed to providing equal employment opportunities to people of all backgrounds and identities.  For more information about staff equity at ANU, click here . For enquiries about the application process, or if you require reasonable adjustment to apply for this role, please contact the hiring manager on the above listed details. Application information In order to apply for this role please make sure that you upload the following documents: A summary addressing your suitability against the selection criteria, that is no more than two pages in length. A current curriculum vitae (CV) which includes the names and contact details of at least three referees (preferably including a current or previous supervisor). If your CV does not include referees you can complete these online when prompted in the application form. Other documents, if required. Applications which do not address the selection criteria may not be considered for the position. Please note: The preferred candidate will be required to complete mandatory pre-employment declarations and background checks relevant to the role they have applied for, in accordance with the Background Checking Procedure and the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-Based Violence . Recommended Jobs Research Fellow Canberra / ACT, ACT, 2601 Seeking a researcher with experience in research and data governance to work on the ARC project ‘Delivering Anindilyakwa data governance' within the School of Demography. Education Systems Support Officer Canberra / ACT, ACT, 2601 Support high-quality engineering education through course administration, educational systems and student-centred processes. Business Analyst Canberra / ACT, ACT, 2601 Support financial management and business development at ACCESS-NRI and contribute to the success of ANU-led national research infrastructure. Coursework Scholarships Coordinator Canberra / ACT, ACT, 2601 Lead coursework scholarship administration, ensuring compliant, student-focused service delivery, governance, and stakeholder support across prestigious scholarship programs. Project Officer Canberra / ACT, ACT, 2601 This is an exceptional chance to be part of the establishment and delivery of a new prestigious Alumni Art Prize – The WILLIAMS. Operations Officer Canberra / ACT, ACT, 2601 The ANU College of Business and Economics is seeking an organised and proactive Operations Officer to support the effective day-to-day operations of the College. The role provides administrative support and advice across student, financial, HR, facilities and general operational matters, while coordinating activities, maintaining accurate records and working with staff and University service areas to resolve issues efficiently."
    },
    "https://jobs.anu.edu.au/jobs/research-fellow-canberra-act-act-australia-2d067816-173c-434b-9b8d-3ffcc5fdc13d": {
      "title": "Research Fellow",
      "description": "Research Fellow - Canberra / ACT, ACT, Australia Privacy Statement People & Culture Information for applicants Salaries & benefits Respect and Inclusion Aboriginal & Torres Strait Islander employment Applicant Login Kiosk mode Research Fellow Research Fellow 563901 Canberra / ACT, ACT, Australia, 2601 Fixed Term Closing at: Nov 15 2026 - 23:55 AEDT Position Description Classification: Academic Level B Salary package: $124,638 - $141,317 per annum plus 17% superannuation Terms: Full-time, Fixed term (up to 2 years) In 1946, ANU was founded to help rebuild a changing world. We’re still at it, 80 years later. For generations, our people have turned curiosity into ideas that have shaped Australia and our region. Learn more about ANU, our history and the community that has shaped us: ANU at 80 The Position The Research Fellow for the School of Demography will provide practical and reliable research for the ARC project ‘Delivering Anindilyakwa data governance' under the direction of the project CIs. The role will support strengthening the capacity of the Data Unit in research capacity, analysis and write-up of project results, and presentations at domestic and international conferences. The Person We are seeking a highly organised and dependable team player with strong attention to detail, research experience and a positive, service-focused approach. A PhD in Demography or related social science discipline is required. You will be confident using standard IT systems, able to manage competing tasks, and comfortable working in a busy academic research environment. Well-developed communication skills, a collaborative mindset and the ability to build good working relationships with all stakeholders are essential. The School/Department The ANU School of Demography is a world-class demographic centre for research and training in the Asia Pacific region. It's core research areas include fertility, family formation and change; mortality, ageing and health; and migration studies. The College/Division The ANU College of Arts and Social Sciences (CASS) is one of seven Colleges at ANU. The College, which is structured into two main research schools, offers degrees in more than 20 discipline areas and excels in research across the creative arts, humanities and social sciences. The College has a substantial international research presence and is a major source of national policy advice. Our academic staff are internationally recognised for their research, and 57 are members of the Australian Academy of the Humanities, the Academy of the Social Sciences of Australia, or both. We also host 13 Australian Research Council Future Fellows and three ARC Laureates. A hub of vibrant activity, we host more than 270 lectures, concerts and exhibitions each year, most of which are open to the public. Our students, staff and graduates come from more than 60 nations, bringing a diversity of perspective to campus life. For further information please contact Professor Brian Houle, T: +61 2 6125 7355, E: brian.houle@anu.edu.au The University actively encourages applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people. For more information on employment opportunities, contact our Indigenous Employment Consultant on: indigenous.employment@anu.edu.au ANU values diversity and inclusion and is committed to providing equal employment opportunities to people of all backgrounds and identities.  For more information about staff equity at ANU, click here . For enquiries about the application process, or if you require reasonable adjustment to apply for this role, please contact the hiring manager on the above listed details. Application information In order to apply for this role please make sure that you upload the following documents: A statement addressing the selection criteria. A current curriculum vitae (CV) which includes the names and contact details of at least three referees (preferably including a current or previous supervisor). If your CV does not include referees you can complete these online when prompted in the application form. Other documents, if required. Applications which do not address the selection criteria may not be considered for the position. Please note: The preferred candidate must have rights to live and work in Australia and will be required to complete mandatory pre-employment declarations and background checks relevant to the role they have applied for, in accordance with the Background Checking Procedure and the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-Based Violence . Recommended Jobs Education Systems Support Officer Canberra / ACT, ACT, 2601 Support high-quality engineering education through course administration, educational systems and student-centred processes. Business Analyst Canberra / ACT, ACT, 2601 Support financial management and business development at ACCESS-NRI and contribute to the success of ANU-led national research infrastructure. Coursework Scholarships Coordinator Canberra / ACT, ACT, 2601 Lead coursework scholarship administration, ensuring compliant, student-focused service delivery, governance, and stakeholder support across prestigious scholarship programs. Project Officer Canberra / ACT, ACT, 2601 This is an exceptional chance to be part of the establishment and delivery of a new prestigious Alumni Art Prize – The WILLIAMS. Postdoctoral / Research Fellow Canberra / ACT, ACT, 2601 Join a vibrant and collaborative environment in Solid Earth Geophysics with world-class expertise in seismology, geodynamics, mathematical geophysics, and rock/mineral physics. Operations Officer Canberra / ACT, ACT, 2601 The ANU College of Business and Economics is seeking an organised and proactive Operations Officer to support the effective day-to-day operations of the College. The role provides administrative support and advice across student, financial, HR, facilities and general operational matters, while coordinating activities, maintaining accurate records and working with staff and University service areas to resolve issues efficiently. Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalise content such as job recommendations, and to analyse our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device I do not accept I accept"
    },
    "https://jobs.anu.edu.au/jobs/lecturer-or-senior-lecturer-up-to-four-positions-available-canberra-act-act-australia": {
      "title": "Lecturer or Senior Lecturer (up to four positions available)",
      "description": "Lecturer or Senior Lecturer (up to four positions available) - Canberra / ACT, ACT, Australia Privacy Statement People & Culture Information for applicants Salaries & benefits Respect and Inclusion Aboriginal & Torres Strait Islander employment Applicant Login Kiosk mode Lecturer or Senior Lecturer (up to four positions available) Lecturer or Senior Lecturer (up to four positions available) 563756 Canberra / ACT, ACT, Australia, 2601 Continuing Closing at: Dec 1 2026 - 23:55 AEDT Add to favourites View favourites Position Description Classification: Academic Level B or C Salary Package: $124,638 - $166,338 per annum plus 17% superannuation Terms: Full-time, continuing Position overview The Mathematical Sciences Institute (MSI), located within the ANU College of Systems and Society (CSS), is seeking to appoint up to four continuing Lecturers and/or Senior Lecturers at Academic Level B and/or Level C, broadly equivalent to Assistant Professor and Associate Professor in the United States. We welcome applications from outstanding mathematicians in any area of mathematics. Applicants should have an excellent research record, relative to opportunity and career stage, and a strong commitment to high-quality teaching. Successful applicants will be expected to develop an internationally visible research program, contribute to the MSI’s undergraduate and postgraduate teaching, supervise research students, and participate in the life of the Institute. In making appointments, MSI will consider both the quality of the candidate and the strength of the research environment available to support their work. The positions include a two-year start-up grant to support research, visitors and conference travel, as well as a reduced teaching load for the first two years. About the Mathematical Sciences Institute The Mathematical Sciences Institute (MSI) is one of Australia’s leading schools for research and education in mathematics. MSI is home to a broad and active research community, with strengths across pure, applied and computational mathematics. Current research areas include algebraic geometry, representation theory, number theory, algebraic and geometric topology, nonlinear partial differential equations, harmonic analysis, geometric analysis, mathematical data science, computational mathematics, mathematical physics, probability and stochastics. The MSI has approximately 51 academics and is located in a modern, award-winning building with excellent research and teaching facilities. MSI offers one of the most comprehensive undergraduate mathematics programs in Australia, as well as Honours, MSc, MPhil and PhD programs. ANU also offers research-focused undergraduate pathways, including the Bachelor of Mathematical Sciences and the elite Bachelor of Philosophy that attracts a significant number of the very best undergraduate students to ANU. MSI supports a large and talented student cohort, with more than 1700 undergraduate coursework students and around 75 students across Honours, MSc, MPhil and PhD programs. MSI also supports students through scholarships, prizes and research opportunities. For further information about MSI, please see our website . Application information All application documentation must be submitted through Australian National University, Mathematical Sciences Institute by 1 December 2026 . Applicants should upload the following documents: A covering letter addressing the selection criteria. A current curriculum vitae, including a publication list. A research and teaching vision statement outlining achievements and future career plans. At least three (3) current letters of recommendation, to be uploaded directly to MathJobs.org by the referees. The Selection Committee intends to conduct first-round Zoom interviews from 14 to 18 December 2026. Shortlisted candidates will be invited to MSI to present a seminar and attend a face-to-face interview between 18 and 28 January 2027. Candidates will be expected to commence within 12 months of accepting an offer. Enquiries about the role and the MSI can be directed to Professor Lilia Ferrario, Director of MSI, via email director.msi@anu.edu.au or phone at +612 6125 2957 What we offer The ANU provides attractive benefits and excellent support to maintain a healthy work/life balance and offers generous remuneration benefits, including four weeks paid vacation per year, assistance with relocation expenses and 17% employer contribution to superannuation. We also offer generous parental leave, the possibility of flexible and part time working arrangements, a parental and aged care support program, dual career hire programs, staff and family tuition fee discounts, ANU school holiday programs, and childcare facilities on campus. For more information, visit: https://services.anu.edu.au/human-resources Our commitment to diversity, belonging, inclusion and equity ANU is committed to building a diverse and inclusive community, and particularly welcomes applications from women, Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people and candidates from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds. Furthermore, it is practice in the ANU College of Systems and Society to actively seek a gender mix of shortlisted candidates for interview. For more information about staff equity at ANU, visit https://services.anu.edu.au/human-resources/respect-inclusion We welcome and develop diversity of backgrounds, experiences and ideas and encourage applications from individuals who may have had non-traditional career paths, who may have taken a career break, had career disruptions or who have achieved excellence in careers outside of the higher education sector. We support applicants who require flexible arrangements in their work environments or patterns. If your experience looks a little different to what we’ve described, but you’re passionate and motivated by this position, we welcome your enquiry and application. Please note: The preferred candidate will be required to complete mandatory pre-employment declarations and background checks relevant to the role they have applied for, in accordance with the Background Checking Procedure and the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-Based Violence . Closing date: Tuesday, 1 December, 2026 11:55PM (AEST) Apply Now First Name (required) e1009cd7 Last Name (required) 4d8c0629 Email (required) c5d1bed3 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Job referral Know someone great for this role! Recommended Jobs Lead Optical Specialist Canberra / ACT, ACT, 2601 Ideal for an experienced optical engineer, this position provides the chance to shape cutting-edge scientific and space technologies while supporting world-leading research and innovation. Mechanical Engineering Specialist Canberra / ACT, ACT, 2601 Join the Advanced Instrumentation and Technology Centre (AITC) to provide specialist mechanical engineering expertise supporting the design, development, validation and maintenance of advanced astronomical instrumentation for world-leading research. Senior Consultant HR Systems Operations Canberra / ACT, ACT, 2601 Oversee operational support for key HR systems, ensuring high-quality service delivery to HR and Payroll stakeholders Associate Professor/ Professor of Music Canberra / ACT, ACT, 2601 An opportunity is available for an outstanding scholar to take up a leadership position at the ANU School of Music working within a collaborative team with world-class researchers and educators. Research Assistant / Research Engineer Canberra / ACT, ACT, 2601 Work with state-of-the-art techniques on AI and Robotics, in collaboration with researchers and practitioners from universities and industry. Research Officer (Peakall) Canberra / ACT, ACT, 2601 Research Officer to perform high quality plant DNA/RNA extraction, library preparation for sequencing and molecular laboratory research support. Job Alerts First Name (required) 0e0ef31e Last Name (required) 92c8edb2 Email (required) a0d8a12d Job Alert 84d4c12a Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Mathematical SciencesInstitute Mathematical SciencesInstitute Categories Academic Academic Employment Type Continuing Continuing Locations Canberra / ACT, ACT, Australia Canberra / ACT, ACT, Australia Classification Level C Level C Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Back to top Acknowledgement of Country The Australian National University acknowledges, celebrates and pays our respects to the Ngunnawal and Ngambri people of the Canberra region and to all First Nations Australians on whose traditional lands we meet and work, and whose cultures are among the oldest continuing cultures in human history. Contact ANU Copyright Disclaimer Privacy Freedom of Information Accessibility TEQSA Provider ID: PRV12002 (Australian University) CRICOS Provider Code: 00120C ABN: 52 234 063 906 MEMBER OF Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalise content such as job recommendations, and to analyse our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device I do not accept I accept Please choose a classification"
